{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed id (Bahasa Indonesia) additions to src/data/claims-lint.json and src/data/keyword-map.json (M3, wave-2 shape). Not merged: the lead merges them.",
    "claimsLint: one entry per claims-lint rule that has per-locale patterns and no id key yet (27 rules; io-home and engine-claim are '*'-only and skipped). Matched like L-14: flags 'iu' on each leaf with placeholders filled and markup stripped; since bb689eb \\w / \\b are Unicode-aware, and the patterns also use explicit (?<![\\p{L}]) / (?![\\p{L}]) where a word edge matters.",
    "keywordMap.seOwned is added to the existing id list ['belajar bahasa Inggris', 'berita bahasa Inggris']; 'kelompok kata' is SurfEnglish's own Indonesian word for chunks (surfenglish.app/id/), like en 'chunks' / pt-BR 'blocos'. Generic learning words without 'Inggris' (pelajar bahasa, belajar bahasa asing) belong to WordByWord (R39, R83) and pass.",
    "keywordMap.reservedG1: how-to phrasing reserved for guide G1 (R46). 'terjemahkan halaman web di iPhone' is deliberately NOT reserved: doc 03 §2.3 table A keeps it as an H1 / body secondary word for the home page.",
    "Tested on the id copy (0 hits, exempt keys aside) and on the counter-examples listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/id-qa.md appendix A."
  ],
